--thirty-two lakhs of योजनस् in extent and encircled by sea of curds (दधिमण्डोद) (क्षीरोद-वि। प्।) of equal dimension; takes its name from a great शाक tree; ruled by a son of Priyavrata, मेधातिथि who divided it among his seven sons and retired to forest; here वायु is wor- shipped by प्राणायाम;
1: भा. V. २०. २४-28.
divided into seven kingdoms bear- ing the respective names of the seven sons of the first king Havya (Bhavya-वि। प्।), a grandson of स्वायम्भुव; con- tains seven streams, several towns and villages; people here follow svadharma and वर्णाश्रम dharma;
2: Br. II. १४. १३; १९. २७, ८०-107; २१. ७३; वा. ३३. १३; ४९. ७४; ५०. १२७.
seven moun- tains;
3: M. १२२. 1.
one of the seven continents, double the size of the क्रौञ्चद्वीप; the four castes in it; Vangas, Magadhas, मानसस् and Mandagas; विष्णु stands in the form of सूर्य.
4: Vi.
